<title>USA: SoftNet Systems unit gets customer contract.</title>
<headline>SoftNet Systems unit gets customer contract.</headline>
<dateline>LAKE FOREST, Ill. 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>SoftNet Systems Inc said Monday its Kansas Communications Inc subsidiary sold a 10-location integrated voice and data system to Harmon Industries Inc.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Harmon produces and supplies signal and train control products for the railroad market. SoftNet develops, markets and installs electronic information and document management systems. Kansas Communications provides communications systems.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
